invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: diff_rsa_ifma
reason: table_select reads the low four bits of the exponent's byte for an
  even digit index and the high four for an odd one, so the window raises
  the base to an exponent with the halves of every byte swapped.
  bin/diff_rsa_ifma holds rsa_ifma_sign_power_pair, word for word, to
  spec/lean/Spec/RsaIfma.lean's signPower, whose digits windowValue_bytes
  proves are the exponent's bytes, which is what makes signPower_eq a proof
  about this file.

--- old
    uint64_t digit = ((uint64_t)e[i >> 1] >> (WINDOW_BITS * (1 - (i & 1)))) & (TABLE_ENTRIES - 1);
--- new
    uint64_t digit = ((uint64_t)e[i >> 1] >> (WINDOW_BITS * (i & 1))) & (TABLE_ENTRIES - 1);
